# Core Engineering

- Prefer clarity over cleverness. Names must reveal intent.
- Change only what the task requires. No drive-by refactors.
- Match existing project patterns before inventing new ones.
- Handle errors explicitly; never swallow exceptions silently.
- Do not hardcode secrets, tokens, or credentials.
- Prefer small, focused functions and modules over large god-objects.
- Add or update tests when changing behavior.
- Document non-obvious decisions in code comments sparingly; prefer self-explanatory code.
- Prefer typed interfaces and validated inputs at system boundaries.
- Keep PRs and commits focused: one concern per change when possible.
